s·gah","gloss":"Pisgah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H6820","lemma":"צֹ֫עַר","tr":"tso·ar","gloss":"Zoar","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H5015","lemma":"נְבוֹ","tr":"ne·vo","gloss":"Nebo","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H1237","lemma":"בִּקְעָה","tr":"biq·ah","gloss":"Valley (of Jericho)","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H0314","lemma":"אַחֲרוֹן","tr":"a·cha·ron","gloss":"last","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":51},{"base":"H5321","lemma":"נַפְתָּלִי","tr":"naph·ta·li","gloss":"Naphtali","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":51},{"base":"H6160","lemma":"עֲרָבָה","tr":"a·ra·vah","gloss":"Arabah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":61},{"base":"H3603","lemma":"כִּכָּר","tr":"kik·kar","gloss":"Plain (of Jericho)","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":68}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":32,"verse":52,"verseEnd":52,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Although you shall see from a distance the land that I am giving the Israelites, you shall not enter it.”","from":4},{"book":"2CH","chapter":28,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then the men who were designated by name arose, took charge of the captives, and provided from the plunder clothing for the naked. They clothed them, gave them sandals and food and drink, anointed their wounds, and put all the feeble on donkeys. So they brought them to Jericho, the City of Palms, to their brothers. Then they returned to Samaria.","from":3},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then the Lordappeared to Abram and said, “I will give this land to your offspring.” So Abram built an altar there to the Lord, who had appeared to him.","from":4},{"book":"JDG","chapter":1,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Now the descendants of Mosesʼ father-in-law, the Kenite, went up with the men of Judah from the City of Palms to the Wilderness of Judah in the Negev near Arad. They went to live among the people.","from":3},{"book":"JDG","chapter":3,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"After enlisting the Ammonites and Amalekites to join forces with him, Eglon attacked and defeated Israel, taking possession of the City of Palms.","from":3},{"book":"DEU","chapter":11,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Every place where the sole of your foot treads will be yours. Your territory will extend from the wilderness to Lebanon, and from the Euphrates River to the Western Sea.","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":13,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"for all the land that you see, I will give to you and your offspring forever.","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"went to war against Bera king of Sodom, Birsha king of Gomorrah, Shinab king of Admah, Shemeber king of Zeboiim, and the king of Bela (that is, Zoar).","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":5}]},"5-8":{"people":[{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":3,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"places":[{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":2,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"beth-peor-h1047","name":"Beth-peor","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"moab-plains-h4124i","name":"Moab Plains","kind":"place","brief":"In Moab","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"words":[{"base":"H1047","lemma":"בֵּית פְּעוֹר","tr":"bet pe·or","gloss":"Beth-peor","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H4872","lemma":"מֹשֶׁה","tr":"mo·sheh","gloss":"Moses","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":766},{"base":"H4124","lemma":"מוֹאָב","tr":"mo·av","gloss":"Moab","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":181},{"base":"H3543","lemma":"כָּהָה","tr":"ka·hah","gloss":"to grow dim","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H4191","lemma":"מוּת","tr":"mut","gloss":"to die","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":840},{"base":"H6900","lemma":"קְבֻרָה","tr":"qe·vu·rah","gloss":"tomb","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H0060","lemma":"אֵ֫בֶל","tr":"e·vel","gloss":"mourning","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H1065","lemma":"בְּכִי","tr":"be·khi","gloss":"weeping","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":30},{"base":"H4136","lemma":"מוּל","tr":"mul","gloss":"opposite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":36},{"base":"H1516","lemma":"גַּיְא","tr":"gay","gloss":"Valley","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":60}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":31,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"he said to them, “I am now a hundred and twenty years old; I am no longer able to come and go, and the LORD has said to me, ‘You shall not cross the Jordan.’","from":7},{"book":"JOS","chapter":14,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"Now behold, as the LORD promised, He has kept me alive these forty-five years since He spoke this word to Moses, while Israel wandered in the wilderness. So here I am today, eighty-five years old,","from":7},{"book":"JOS","chapter":14,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"still as strong today as I was the day Moses sent me out. As my strength was then, so it is now for war, for going out, and for coming in.","from":7},{"book":"JUD","chapter":1,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"But even the archangel Michael, when he disputed with the devil over the body of Moses, did not presume to bring a slanderous charge against him, but said, “The Lord rebuke you!”","from":6},{"book":"GEN","chapter":27,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"When Isaac was old and his eyes were so weak that he could no longer see, he called his older son Esau and said to him, “My son.” “Here I am,” Esau replied.","from":7},{"book":"GEN","chapter":48,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Now Israelʼs eyesight was poor because of old age; he could hardly see. Joseph brought his sons to him, and his father kissed them and embraced them.","from":7},{"book":"ACT","chapter":7,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"He led them out and performed wonders and signs in the land of Egypt, at the Red Sea, and for forty years in the wilderness.","from":7},{"book":"GEN","chapter":50,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"taking the forty days required to complete the embalming. And the Egyptians mourned for him seventy days.","from":8}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"9-12":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":3,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"nun-h5126","name":"Nun","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Joshua","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547j","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":1,"firstVerse":11}],"places":[{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11}],"words":[{"base":"H4872","lemma":"מֹשֶׁה","tr":"mo·sheh","gloss":"Moses","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":766},{"base":"H4172","lemma":"מוֹרָא","tr":"mo·ra","gloss":"fear","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H5126","lemma":"נוּן","tr":"nun","gloss":"Nun","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":30},{"base":"H4159","lemma":"מוֹפֵת","tr":"mo·phet","gloss":"wonder","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":36},{"base":"H5564","lemma":"סָמַךְ","tr":"sa·makh","gloss":"to support","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":48},{"base":"H2389","lemma":"חָזָק","tr":"cha·zaq","gloss":"strong","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":56},{"base":"H4392","lemma":"מָלֵא","tr":"ma·le","gloss":"full","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":64},{"base":"H0226","lemma":"אוֹת","tr":"ot","gloss":"sign: miraculous","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":79},{"base":"H2451","lemma":"חׇכְמָה","tr":"chokh·mah","gloss":"wisdom","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":153},{"base":"H3091","lemma":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","tr":"ye·ho·shu·a","gloss":"Joshua","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":218}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ISA","chapter":11,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"The Spirit of the LORD will rest on Him— the Spirit of wisdom and understanding, the Spirit of counsel and strength, the Spirit of knowledge and fear of the LORD.","from":9},{"book":"EXO","chapter":33,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Thus the LORD would speak to Moses face to face, as a man speaks to his friend. Then Moses would return to the camp, but his young assistant Joshua son of Nun would not leave the tent.","from":10},{"book":"DAN","chapter":6,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Soon, by his extraordinary spirit, Daniel distinguished himself among the administrators and satraps. So the king planned to set him over the whole kingdom.","from":9},{"book":"JHN","chapter":3,"verse":34,"verseEnd":34,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"For the One whom God has sent speaks the words of God, for God gives the Spirit without limit.","from":9},{"book":"ACT","chapter":6,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"They presented these seven to the apostles, who prayed and laid their hands on them.","from":9},{"book":"ACT","chapter":8,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Then Peter and John laid their hands on them, and they received the Holy Spirit.","from":9},{"book":"ACT","chapter":8,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"“Give me this power as well,” he said, “so that everyone on whom I lay my hands may receive the Holy Spirit.”","from":9},{"book":"1KI","chapter":3,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Therefore give Your servant an understanding heart to judge Your people and to discern between good and evil. For who is able to govern this great people of Yours?”","from":9}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":3}]}}